+\begin{lemma}[Magnetization from the equation of state]
+\label{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:magnetization_of_eos}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.magnetization_of_eos}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:TorusParams, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:WorkingState, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:ParamagnetEOS}
+The equation of state determines the magnetization from the field:
+off $T \neq 0$, $M = (n\,K\,H)/(V\,T)$ --- the transport form of the
+EOS used when the isothermal heat relation is moved between $H$-data
+and $M$-data. This is the intended role of the EOS packaging: an
+elimination form constraining the model.
+\end{lemma}
+\begin{proof}
+Rearrange $T\,M\,V = n\,K\,H$ by dividing by $V\,T \neq 0$
+($V > 0$ from the torus parameters, $T \neq 0$ by hypothesis).
+\end{proof}
+
+\begin{lemma}[Heat leaves the torus on field increase]
+\label{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:heat_leaves_torus_on_field_increase}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.heat_leaves_torus_on_field_increase}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:TorusParams, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:IsothermalHeatIntoTorus}
+Sign content of the isothermal heat relation: when the field is
+increased at fixed positive temperature ($0 \le H_i < H_f$, $T > 0$),
+the heat into the torus is negative, $Q < 0$ --- the orientation of
+the $3 \to 4$ leg of Figure~3b, and the reason $Q_h$ is a heat
+\emph{delivered to} the hot reservoir.
+\end{lemma}
+\begin{proof}
+In $Q = -(\mu_0 n K/(2T))\,(H_f^{\,2} - H_i^{\,2})$ the prefactor is
+strictly positive (all torus parameters and $T$ positive) and
+$H_f^{\,2} - H_i^{\,2} > 0$ for $0 \le H_i < H_f$; the leading minus
+sign forces $Q < 0$.
+\end{proof}
+
+\subsection*{Derivation bridges: per-cycle densities}
+
+\begin{lemma}[Heat-dumped density]
+\label{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:heatDumpedDensity_eq}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.heatDumpedDensity_eq}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:globalQuantities, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:CoolingRun, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:CarnotHeatRatio, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:BodyCalorimeterDensityLaw, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:IsCoolingRun}
+Per-cycle heat dumped to the hot reservoir, in density form: at every
+control temperature $T' \in (T, T_0)$ of a cooling run,
+$\delta Q_h/\Delta T' = C_c\,T_h/T'$.
+\end{lemma}
+\begin{proof}
+Divide the product-form Carnot ratio
+$(\delta Q_h/\Delta T')\,T' = (\delta Q_c/\Delta T')\,T_h$ by
+$T' \neq 0$ and substitute the calorimetric law
+$\delta Q_c/\Delta T' = C_c$.
+\end{proof}
+
+\begin{lemma}[Work density]
+\label{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:workDensity_eq}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.workDensity_eq}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:globalQuantities, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:CoolingRun, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:CycleWorkHeatBalance, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:BodyCalorimeterDensityLaw, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:IsCoolingRun, lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:heatDumpedDensity_eq}
+Per-cycle work density: at every control temperature
+$T' \in (T, T_0)$ of a cooling run,
+$\delta W/\Delta T' = C_c\,(T_h/T' - 1)$.
+\end{lemma}
+\begin{proof}
+First law
+$\delta W/\Delta T' = \delta Q_h/\Delta T' - \delta Q_c/\Delta T'$;
+substitute the heat-dumped density $C_c\,T_h/T'$ and the calorimetric
+law $C_c$, then factor $C_c$.
+\end{proof}
+
+\begin{lemma}[Residence-time density]
+\label{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:residenceDensity_eq}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.residenceDensity_eq}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:globalQuantities, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:CoolingRun, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:ConstantPowerDensityLaw, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:IsCoolingRun, lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:workDensity_eq}
+Residence-time density: at every control temperature
+$T' \in (T, T_0)$ of a cooling run,
+$\delta s/\Delta T' = (C_c/P)\,(T_h/T' - 1)$ --- the informal
+differential relation $P\,ds = C_c\,(T_h/T' - 1)\,(-dT')$ with the
+cooling branch ($\Delta T' > 0$ per drop) built in.
+\end{lemma}
+\begin{proof}
+Divide the constant-power law
+$\delta W/\Delta T' = P\,\delta s/\Delta T'$ by $P > 0$ (regime) and
+substitute the work-density identity.
+\end{proof}
+
+\subsection*{Value theorems: accumulation and the C.4 elapsed time}
+
+\begin{theorem}[Accumulation bridge: $t$ as the residence-density integral]
+\label{thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:elapsedTime_eq_integral}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.elapsedTime_eq_integral}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:globalQuantities, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:RegimeAssumptions, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:CoolingRun, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:IsCoolingRun, lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:residenceDensity_eq}
+The elapsed time of the cooling run, defined operationally as the
+integral of the residence-time density over the visited temperatures
+(additivity of time over the run, hypothesis \texttt{haccum}), equals
+the integral of the explicit residence density:
+$t = \int_{T' \in [T,\,T_0]} (C_c/P)\,(T_h/T' - 1)\,dT'$.
+\end{theorem}
+\begin{proof}
+Rewrite the integrand by the residence-density identity on the open
+interval $(T, T_0)$; set-integral congruence extends the rewrite to
+the closed interval since the two endpoints form a measure-zero set.
+\end{proof}
+
+\begin{theorem}[Evaluation bridge: the residence-time integral]
+\label{thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:cooling_time_integral_eval}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.cooling_time_integral_eval}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:globalQuantities, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:RegimeAssumptions}
+The residence-time integral evaluates in closed form:
+$\int_{[T,\,T_0]} (C_c/P)\,(T_h/T' - 1)\,dT'
+= (C_c/P)\,\bigl(T_h\,\ln(T_0/T) - (T_0 - T)\bigr)$.
+(Conclusion-side intermediate value; not the official C.4 answer
+form.)
+\end{theorem}
+\begin{proof}
+Fundamental theorem of calculus on $0 < T \le T' \le T_0$:
+$\int T_h/T' \, dT' = T_h \ln(T_0/T)$ off $T' \neq 0$ and
+$\int 1\,dT' = T_0 - T$; pull the constant $C_c/P$ out.
+\end{proof}
+
+\begin{theorem}[Subquestion C.4: elapsed cooling time]
+\label{thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:c4_elapsed_time}
+\lean{IPhO2026.Problem3.C4.c4_elapsed_time}
+\uses{def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:globalQuantities, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:RegimeAssumptions, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:CoolingRun, def:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:IsCoolingRun, thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:elapsedTime_eq_integral, thm:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_3_C_4:cooling_time_integral_eval}
+The body of heat capacity $C_c$, cooled from $T_0$ to $T$ at constant
+input power $P$ and constant hot-reservoir temperature $T_h$, reaches
+$T$ in elapsed time
+\[
+t = \frac{C_c\,T_h}{P}\Bigl(\ln\frac{T_0}{T} - \frac{T_0 - T}{T_h}\Bigr).
+\]
+The right-hand side is the recorded official answer of subquestion
+C.4; it is purely conclusion-side --- the hypotheses only bundle the
+per-cycle governing laws (the cooling-run predicate, composed of the
+Carnot heat ratio, the first law, the constant-power law, and the
+calorimetric law) and the operational definition of the elapsed time.
+\end{theorem}
+\begin{proof}
+Chain the accumulation bridge with the evaluation bridge, then apply
+the field algebra
+$(C_c/P)\,(T_h \ln(T_0/T) - (T_0 - T))
+= (C_c T_h/P)\,(\ln(T_0/T) - (T_0 - T)/T_h)$,
+factoring $T_h$ out of the parenthesis.
+\end{proof}
